-## 6. Pairs Well With
+## 6. PostTrainingX B200 shutdown qualification
+
+The separate `run_qwen3_6_35b_a3b_posttrainingx.py` launcher offers
+`--release-pinned-backups-on-exit` (default off). It requires
+`--rollout-journal-dir` and Megatron without a critic. After the normal
+save/update/evaluation/dispose path, each trainer rank releases its actor/reference
+CPU weight backups and flushes the pinned host allocator cache. Model, optimizer,
+scheduler and CUDA/NCCL contexts are not modified by this cleanup. Backup access
+after release is an error, so this must not be used between training steps.
+
+Started/completed/failed receipts include rank, policy version, timing and allocator
+bytes in the private journal. Missing allocator support or incomplete release fails
+the run. The four-node memory control passed with explicit release, but this option
+still requires full-trainer validation; it does not relax any telemetry deadline.
+
+## 7. Pairs Well With
 
 - [Speculative Decoding](/advanced/speculative-decoding)
 - [Backends Beyond Megatron](/advanced/architecture-support)
